WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.249
The kids rushed down the hill to Mango.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.505
He was lying in a crumpled heap.

3
00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:10.867
"Are you okay?" Ezra asked.

4
00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:15.666
"I twisted my ankle." Mango tried to stand up.

5
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.499
"Owie, owie!"

6
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.958
"Can you walk on it at all?" Ivy asked.

7
00:00:21.959 --> 00:00:27.448
Mango rubbed his ankle. "Owie, owie."

8
00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:30.839
"This is all your fault!" Huck yelled at Buck.

9
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.841
"You pushed me into Mango."

10
00:00:33.842 --> 00:00:38.416
"It's your fault for being so clumsy!" Buck yelled back.

11
00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:43.197
Ivy rolled her eyes as the Ucks kept fighting.

12
00:00:43.198 --> 00:00:48.291
"Mango, what should we do to help you?" Ezra asked.

13
00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:50.624
Mango opened his mouth.

14
00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:54.124
The kids leaned forward, waiting for instructions.

15
00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:58.599
"Owie, owie!" was all Mango could say.

16
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.587
"What are we going to do?" Ezra sounded panicked.

17
00:01:02.588 --> 00:01:05.041
"Mango can't walk.

18
00:01:05.042 --> 00:01:09.884
And it's against camp rules for campers to hike without a counselor."

19
00:01:09.885 --> 00:01:12.341
He looked around at the woods.

20
00:01:12.342 --> 00:01:18.006
"We're stuck here! We'll have to fight off bears! And

21
00:01:18.007 --> 00:01:25.772
eat tree bark to survive!" "Everyone,

22
00:01:25.773 --> 00:01:29.776
calm down," Glen said. To

23
00:01:29.777 --> 00:01:33.916
Ivy's surprise, everyone turned to him. "Ucks,"

24
00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:37.754
Glen said. "Stop arguing. You're

25
00:01:37.755 --> 00:01:43.166
big enough to help Mango walk." "Hey!

26
00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:47.832
Who put you in charge?" Chuck said. "I

27
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:57.249
did," Mango said. "Somebody has to take over for me. Owie!" Buck

28
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.194
and Huck got on either side of Mango. He

29
00:02:00.196 --> 00:02:02.785
swung his arms over their shoulders. They

30
00:02:02.786 --> 00:02:05.334
all took slow steps. Mango

31
00:02:05.335 --> 00:02:08.749
hopped along on one foot. "See—no

32
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.712
reason to panic," Glen said. "Now

33
00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:15.440
we just walk back to camp. Come

34
00:02:15.441 --> 00:02:19.435
on, everyone. Follow me." All

35
00:02:19.436 --> 00:02:23.999
the campers got behind Glen and started walking. Ivy

36
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.207
and Ezra exchanged astonished looks. "What

37
00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:30.824
just happened?" Ezra asked. "Since

38
00:02:30.825 --> 00:02:35.523
when does Glen actually know what to do?" Ivy

39
00:02:35.524 --> 00:02:41.839
shook her head. "I have no idea. Hey, Glen!" She

40
00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:48.250
caught up to him. "Wow! You took charge like a real leader." "Really?

41
00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:53.539
Me—a leader ?" Glen chuckled.

42
00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.709
"I guess you're right." He stood up straighter.

43
00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:04.291
"I'm the leader of this group!" He threw his shoulders back and marched forward.

44
00:03:04.292 --> 00:03:09.212
Ezra moaned. "You shouldn't have said that, Ivy.

45
00:03:09.213 --> 00:03:11.974
You know how Glen gets.

46
00:03:11.975 --> 00:03:16.797
He'll brag about taking charge for the rest of the summer."

47
00:03:16.798 --> 00:03:20.454
"Oops." Ivy looked sheepish.

48
00:03:20.456 --> 00:03:25.592
"You're right, Ezra. I hope I haven't created a monster."

49
00:03:25.593 --> 00:03:34.166
Ezra sighed. "Me too. I'm the one who has to share a cabin with him."

50
00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:39.207
*** It took awhile, but the hikers finally arrived back at

51
00:03:39.208 --> 00:03:43.106
camp. When Private saw them, she rushed

52
00:03:43.107 --> 00:03:48.198
over. "We expected you back half an hour ago. What

53
00:03:48.199 --> 00:03:51.681
happened?" "I fell and twisted my ankle," Mango

54
00:03:51.682 --> 00:03:56.119
said. "We could have been stranded in the woods for hours. But . .

55
00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.178
." He patted Glen's head.

56
00:03:58.179 --> 00:04:03.499
"But my little hero here organized everyone to get us back safely."

57
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.479
Private looked at Glen and gave him a salute.

58
00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.756
"Congratulations, camper.

59
00:04:08.757 --> 00:04:14.166
It sounds like you seized control of a very dangerous situation."

60
00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:17.255
"Thanks." Glen frowned.

61
00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:21.249
"But I wouldn't call myself a little hero.

62
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:26.806
What I did was pretty big—I'd call it huge, in fact!"

63
00:04:26.807 --> 00:04:30.232
"Uh-oh," Ivy thought.

64
00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:34.899
"There we were, surrounded by danger," Glen went on.

65
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.957
"All of the less experienced hikers were panicking.

66
00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:43.904
Ezra was so hungry, he started eating tree bark!"

67
00:04:43.905 --> 00:04:47.051
"What?" Ezra squawked.

68
00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:51.665
Private frowned. "That's very bad for your teeth, camper.

69
00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:55.071
And it can't be good for the tree either."

70
00:04:55.072 --> 00:05:00.606
"No, I . . . didn't!" Ezra said. "I—"

71
00:05:00.607 --> 00:05:06.476
"I knew I had to take charge, or we'd never survive!" Glen said.

72
00:05:06.477 --> 00:05:13.040
"I saved these campers from a fate worse than death!"

